         One stage in its limit with the others at the largest state: 25.112 A.
    WHICH ONE THE DECLARATION HOLDS, AND WHY: the peak holds (i), named an upper bound in its note; the typical holds the sum of the
    leads' typicals; the loads stay the union of the leads' allocations, with the PoE return added.
      - (i) is the only figure that is true by construction: the return cannot carry more than its leads are declared to carry,
        and those declarations are Layer 5's contract at both ends of each lead. Derived in the generator, it follows a lead
        that is declared again; typed, it went stale on 28 September (S-98) and again with fans12.
      - (ii) against (i), like for like (the PoE stage is off in the budget, so the 5 V leads alone): with Layer 9's draft composed
        the largest state with every start at once is 26.283 A against 27.18 A: inside. Without that draft it is 26.283 A against
        25.80 A: OVER by 0.483 A, because the device lead declares 6.0 A where C-DEV rev 1 has 7.4717 A. That is I-03 itself
        (OPEN, Layer 9's): the return follows what that lead declares and does not paper over it.
      - (iii) is a fault current of four independent limits at once; intent.py's own rule puts a fault current in the note,
        not in the peak (the barrel rule PI-003 reads the peak). One stage in its limit is inside (i).
      - what the peak is NOT: a claim that 27.78 A flows. The copper rules solve the return's mesh at the declared loads,
        22.113 A with the PoE return; the peak is what a barrel is judged at.

3. THE CAPACITY BASIS
3a. THE GROUND CONDUCTORS BETWEEN BOARDS A AND B, read on both committed netlists (v2/ecad/pcb-a-power-a23/out/pcb-a-power.net, v2/ecad/pcb-b-compute-b19/out/pcb-b-compute.net):
      lead contacts, pin 2 on GND: board A J_54V, J_5V_DEV, J_5V_S1, J_5V_S2, J_5V_S3; board B J_54V, J_5V_DEV, J_5V_S1, J_5V_S2, J_5V_S3: the same five
      ribbon conductors on GND: J_AB1 pins 3,4,5,6,7,8,22,23,24 (board A) and 3,4,5,6,7,8,22,23,24 (board B); J_AB2 pins 3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10 and 3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10: 17 conductors, the same on both boards
      so the two boards' grounds are ONE net joined by five lead contacts and seventeen ribbon conductors in parallel (six leads
      with Layer 9's draft). Nothing makes a lead's pin 2 carry its own rail's current: the return divides by resistance.
      NOT IN THE MODEL (each takes current off the conductors below; none has a held resistance): the shields of the GNSS and
      LoRa pigtails if board A bonds its jacks to GND, and each board's own plane resistance, taken as one node a board.
3b. THE MAKERS' PRINTED FIGURES
      JST VH (v2/vendor/connectors/jst-vh-catalogue.pdf, catalogue, revision not printed): 10 A 'when using AWG #16 with the standard type header' (PRINTED); 7 A
        'when using AWG #18 with the shrouded type header' (PRINTED; the fitted B2P-VH is the standard header, so J_54V's AWG 18 lead
        has NO STATED RATING, Layer 5's own INCONCLUSIVE); range to +105 C including the rise (PRINTED); contact resistance 10 mOhm
        maximum initial, 20 mOhm after test (PRINTED; NO MINIMUM and no typical); conductors 1.25 mm2 (AWG 16) and 0.83 mm2 (AWG 18)
        (PRINTED). Its note (PRINTED): 'Do not branch in parallel current which exceeds the rated current. If branched in parallel,
        current imbalance or other problems may occur. If it is absolutely necessary to branch such a large current in parallel,
        design the circuits without causing any imbalance and provide extra margin for each circuit.'
      Wurth WR-CAB ribbon (v2/vendor/connectors/wurth-wr-cab-ribbon-63912615521cab.pdf): rated current 1 A a conductor at 25 C ambient, 'the current rating may decrease due to the derating
        effect at higher temperatures' with no curve (PRINTED); conductor resistance 237 Ohm/km maximum, AWG 28 (PRINTED).
      Wurth WR-BHD IDC socket (v2/vendor/connectors/wurth-wr-bhd-idc-socket-61202623021.pdf): 1 A a contact, contact resistance 20 mOhm maximum (PRINTED). Box header: 3 A at 25 C (PRINTED).
      THE INSIDE AIR (L4-E12, MODELED): 71.25 C in E3-O, 76.25 C in E5's dwell. The VH contact may add 28.75 K at 76.25 C before its range's
        top. The catalogue prints no rise at 10 A and no derating curve: if that rise is 30 K (ASSUMPTION) the contact carries
        9.789 A at 76.25 C; the printed 10 A is what the rows below are judged at, and this figure is shown beside it. The budget's
        largest state at E5's air is a conservative pairing: L4-E12's states at that air run less than PS-ALLTX.
