3h. BOARD A'S END. Its committed generator declares GND as a node, which no copper rule solves; this record's round 3 draft (apply_gen_sch_a_packrtn.py) declares it
    a rail returning CELL+ from the dock contacts to the stages' input ends at the pack's 18.0 A. Neither says that the 5 V returns
    enter at J_5V_S1..3, J_5V_DEV and J_54V pin 2 and at the ribbons and close at each stage's output: intent.rail has one set of
    sources and takes no current entering at a load, so the rule set cannot solve that loop on board A as it stands (finding
    L8R2-F33: the same currents and the same layout constraint as board B's, stated for board A's layout).
3i. LAYER 5'S CONTRACT ROWS (v2/ecad/tools/pcb_interfaces.yaml). IF-AB-POWER: harness 'JST-VH pairs, 16 AWG on the four 5 V leads and 18 AWG on J_54V, 150 mm (cable; ASSEMBLY.md section 4)'; pins '1 = the rail, 2 = GND, on both ends'; its currents rows declare each rail lead by lead
    (5.0, 5.63 and 6.0 A peaks, INTERIM) and its contact_rating reads the 10 A as this record does. It carries NO ROW for the return's
    division, and IF-AB-RIBBON and IF-AB-WALL declare their ground pins as signal returns at 1 A a contact. The row texts this
    round proposes are in the record's section 3g (Layer 5's files are its own).
3j. THE CORRECTIONS COMPARED on the upper bound with Layer 9's draft (27.78 A, six leads; every contact case K0 to K5; the worse of
    20 C and 76.25 C; MODEL):
    A0 MORE VH RETURN CONTACTS (the plain remedy): with every return an AWG 16 lead of 150 mm, the rows that take the contacts at
       their initial maxima (K0, K1, K3, K4) hold from 14 contacts, and every row (the after-test maxima too) from 24, against
       the six drawn. Not a small correction: REJECTED.
    A1 A DEDICATED GROUND RETURN between the two boards' grounds (a strap on bolted lands, or the bay spacers bonded to both
       grounds), R_s end to end with its joints: every row is inside the printed ratings (a VH contact 10 A, a ribbon conductor
       1 A) while R_s is at or under 2.34 mOhm; with a ribbon conductor held to 0.5 A (RIB_DERATE, ASSUMPTION) while R_s is at or
       under 0.53 mOhm. The added return then carries up to 22.8 A and needs its own rating and a bond-resistance check at
       assembly. It takes the dependence on the VH contacts away: no contact case fails.
    A2 THE RIBBONS' GROUND CONDUCTORS BALLASTED (1 Ohm in series with each, on one board; an illustration): a ribbon conductor
       carries at most 0.173 A in every row; the leads then carry the whole return, 4.875 A a contact with equal contacts and
       18.562 A on the extreme K3 (BOUND, over the printed 10 A). The ribbons are protected on printed figures; the lead contacts
       are left to JST's 'no imbalance' and 'extra margin'; every ribbon signal's return gains that impedance (the signal
       return rules RET-001 to RET-003 would have to be re-read).
    A3 NO CIRCUIT CHANGE, a harness acceptance: every VH contact at or under 4.16 mOhm for the ribbons and 3.24 mOhm for the leads
       (3e at this total), under the maker's own 10 mOhm limit, measured four-wire at assembly and again as the contacts age. An
       assigned test is not a corrected circuit.
    SELECTED AS THE DIRECTION (authority SESSION): A1. Reason: it is the one approach under which every row holds on the makers'
       printed maxima, it leaves the signal ribbons' returns as they are, and its own unknown (the joints) is a bond resistance
       a four-wire reading at assembly settles. NOT DRAFTED in this round: it adds a land and a part on boards A and B, a
       strap or spacer row (Layer 7), a contract row (Layer 5), and it must be read against GND-002's single chassis bond
       (record l8gnd: joining the two boards' grounds is no second bond; touching the plate would be). To reverse: take A2 or A3
       in L4-E9's register. L8R2-F31 stays OPEN until a draft composes, is read on both netlists and holds these rows.

4. THE JUDGMENT
   (a) THE DECLARATION IS WRONG, and is corrected (section 5). Its peak was a typed sum of the leads' peaks that went stale twice;
       its typical 10.0 A is under the leads' own 13.30 A; its sources omit J_54V. The basis supports: typical 13.30 A and peak 26.40 A
       (27.78 A with Layer 9's draft), derived in the generator from the leads' declarations, the peak an UPPER BOUND.
   (b) THE LOAD LIST IS RIGHT IN WHAT IT COUNTS AND MISSED ONE RETURN: no ampere is counted twice and none returns elsewhere; the PoE
       port's 0.60 A at R12 is added. Against Layer 9's budget the device rail's ALLOCATIONS (5.49 A) and its declared 6.0 A peak are
       under C-DEV rev 1's 7.4717 A: that is I-03 (OPEN), corrected by Layer 9's draft, not by this round.
   (c) THE RETURN PATH DOES NOT HOLD ON THE MAKERS' PRINTED FIGURES: a circuit defect of the A to B interface, finding L8R2-F31,
       OPEN. The return is branched in parallel over five (six) VH contacts and the seventeen ground conductors of two signal
       ribbons, and nothing sets its division.
       - New contacts at one value (K0, K1): every conductor is inside its printed rating at every total.
       - VH contacts aged to JST's own after-test limit, still equal (K2): a ribbon conductor carries 0.959 A at Layer 9's largest
         state, inside its printed 1 A at 25 C by 4.1 % in air where its maker states a derating and prints no curve; and
         1.101 A at the upper bound, over it.
       - Unequal contacts inside the makers' limits (K3 to K5, BOUNDS): at the largest state already a ribbon conductor reads
         1.195 A and a lead contact 11.7 A; at the upper bound 1.41 A and 13.5 A.
       The division holds only while the VH contacts stay under 2.8 to 6.8 mOhm, better than their maker's 10 mOhm limit (3e);
       JST's note asks a parallel branch to be designed 'without causing any imbalance' with 'extra margin for each circuit',
       and the ribbons' contracts never counted supply current. These are the MODEL's answers on printed maxima: no harness
       exists and no contact has been measured, so they are not a measured overload, and a balanced reading is not evidence
       either. More return contacts close it only from 24 VH contacts in place of six (3j, A0); 3j scopes the correction (A1,
       a dedicated return, selected as the direction; not drafted: boards A and B, the harness and two contracts).
   NOT RAISED TO MAKE THE GENERATOR PASS: the declaration is derived, the same text reads 22.23 A on the committed generator, a lead
       declared lower lowers it, and the capacity finding stays OPEN beside it.

