     labels: pin 1 is each rail's own current (J_54V's 0: the PoE stage is off in PS-ALLTX; 0.60 A DECLARED peak when the outlet is on);
     pin 2 is the SAME total divided by resistance, so J_5V_IOC's pin 2 carries about a sixth of the leads' share whatever U601
     supplies, and 'J_5V_DEV's return falls by the same current' (record l9t5's line) holds for pin 1 and not for pin 2. The J_5V_IOC
     lead's gauge and length are ASSUMPTIONS here (AWG 16, 150 mm): record l9t5's draft names neither.
     On Layer 9's own rounds 4 and 5 (PS-ALLTX with the standby card off) slot 3 reads 3.396 A and the total 20.9497 A; every row above
     scales by 0.9113.
   CREDIT (the common brief's three criteria) for this round's two drafts: (a) composes in L4-E9's order and the generator runs: yes;
   (b) the changed declaration read on the regenerated netlist and intent with mutations that fail: yes; (c) electrical acceptance on
   the makers' printed figures: the DECLARATION is supported as an upper bound (section 2c); the RETURN PATH does not hold on
   the makers' printed figures (section 3, L8R2-F31 OPEN): NOT accepted. A netlist check is not electrical qualification.

